<title>BELGIUM: W. Europe car registrations down 1.3 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>W. Europe car registrations down 1.3 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>New passenger car registrations in western Europe fell 1.3 percent in February to 1,039,300 compared with the same month last year, the European car manufacturers' association (ACEA) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>New car registrations declined 1.8 percent to 2,178,100 units in the first two months of the year compared with the January-February period in 1996, ACEA said.</p>
<p>Western Europe includes the 15 European Union countries, Norway, Switzerland and Liechtenstein.</p>
<p>-- Fredrik Dahl +32 2 287 68 11</p>
</text>
